    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16582" root="رم" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَمَّةٌ</span></b>  [originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْمَمَةٌ</span>, a noun of the same class
as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَجْنبَنَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَبْخَلَةٌ</span> &amp;c., meaning <i>A cause of
repair:</i> and hence, <i>a thing needing repair;</i> as
in a phrase mentioned voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَقِيعٌ</span>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَمَّةُ بَيْتِ</span>, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُمٌّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And see what here follows.

